WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.534 --> 00:00:18.544
"Danger for all Reds?" Gliss cried, echoing the crow's warning. "What does that mean?"

2
00:00:18.545 --> 00:00:23.469
"Hush," Professor Liblow said again. "Let it finish its message."

3
00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:25.946
Echo crows didn't talk on their own.

4
00:00:25.947 --> 00:00:28.824
They could only repeat what a person told them.

5
00:00:28.825 --> 00:00:32.890
The crow flapped its wings. "Urgent danger," it said again.

6
00:00:32.891 --> 00:00:38.537
"Reds are disappearing all over Magica. Nobody knows where they went or what has become of them.

7
00:00:38.538 --> 00:00:43.030
All Reds, please take precautions. Urgent, urgent."

8
00:00:43.031 --> 00:00:47.422
The echo crow clacked its beak. Then it flew out of the room.

9
00:00:47.423 --> 00:00:52.676
Everyone started talking at once. Well, almost everyone.

10
00:00:52.677 --> 00:00:57.243
Zann didn't say a word. The crow's message had made him think about his parents.

11
00:00:57.244 --> 00:01:00.779
Nobody knew where they were either, or what had become of them.

12
00:01:00.780 --> 00:01:04.167
But that was different. For one thing, they weren't Reds.

13
00:01:04.168 --> 00:01:08.352
For another, they had disappeared four long years ago.

14
00:01:08.353 --> 00:01:14.288
Perda poked him. "Did you hear that?" she said. "What do you think it means?"

15
00:01:14.289 --> 00:01:22.080
"Silence!" Professor Liblow cried. His voice boomed, with the help of a Swelling spell.

16
00:01:22.081 --> 00:01:26.038
The class quieted down at once. Gliss raised her hand.

17
00:01:26.039 --> 00:01:29.356
"I need to go home," she said, her voice cracking.

18
00:01:29.357 --> 00:01:34.650
"Both of my parents are Reds. I should tell them about this warning!"

19
00:01:34.651 --> 00:01:39.490
"Me too," Zann said. "My grandfather, Boz, is a Red."

20
00:01:39.491 --> 00:01:44.713
"What's the big deal?" Jev's voice was loud enough for Zann to hear, but not the teacher.

21
00:01:44.714 --> 00:01:48.993
"All those snooty Reds are probably sneaking off somewhere together.

22
00:01:48.994 --> 00:01:54.014
Maybe they're trying to come up with even more ways to act superior to the rest of us."

23
00:01:54.015 --> 00:01:59.383
"Be quiet, Jev." Perda glared at him. "You're just jealous."

24
00:01:59.384 --> 00:02:05.323
Gliss hadn't heard Jev. She stood up. "I just remembered something," she said.

25
00:02:05.324 --> 00:02:08.714
"Last night I overheard my parents whispering."

26
00:02:08.715 --> 00:02:15.225
"You overheard them?" Professor Liblow gave her a suspicious look. "How?"

27
00:02:15.226 --> 00:02:19.666
Gliss blushed. "Okay, I admit it. I used a spy fly.

28
00:02:19.667 --> 00:02:22.816
I know we're not supposed to use them to spy on people.

29
00:02:22.817 --> 00:02:26.471
But my parents wouldn't tell me why they look so worried lately.

30
00:02:26.472 --> 00:02:29.528
I had to find out what's going on!"

31
00:02:29.529 --> 00:02:35.674
"Wow," thought Zann. If Gliss had used a spy fly, she must have been very concerned.

32
00:02:35.675 --> 00:02:38.600
"So what did you hear?" he asked.

33
00:02:38.601 --> 00:02:42.997
"It was about my uncle," Gliss said. "He lives in New Mist."

34
00:02:42.998 --> 00:02:46.355
"You mean the town near Mount Mystery?" Zann said.

35
00:02:46.356 --> 00:02:53.090
"My parents haven't heard from Uncle Gar in three days," Gliss said. "He's a Red too."

36
00:02:53.091 --> 00:02:59.149
"Oh dear." Professor Liblow shook his head. "This sounds rather serious.

37
00:02:59.150 --> 00:03:04.685
Perhaps you'd better go home . . . It's almost time to go anyway. Class dismissed."

38
00:03:04.686 --> 00:03:08.944
The students started gathering their things and chattering about what had just happened.

39
00:03:08.945 --> 00:03:14.486
Zann grabbed his bag and hurried out of the room with Perda.

40
00:03:14.487 --> 00:03:18.317
"I should find out what Boz knows about this," Zann said.

41
00:03:18.318 --> 00:03:25.266
"He's a retired Magic Master, remember? Maybe some of his friends in the capital know what's going on."

42
00:03:25.267 --> 00:03:29.807
Perda gave him a look. "You sound almost excited," she said.

43
00:03:29.808 --> 00:03:33.134
"Aren't you scared? You and Boz are both Reds."

44
00:03:33.135 --> 00:03:37.645
Before Zann could respond, Jev came into the hall with some friends.

45
00:03:37.646 --> 00:03:42.012
"Rushing home to hide under your bed, Red?" Jev jeered.

46
00:03:42.013 --> 00:03:51.485
Zann didn't answer. Jev had never forgiven him for an incident on Zann's first day at the Swamp Bottom School almost four years earlier.

47
00:03:51.486 --> 00:03:57.778
But even if that had never happened, they still wouldn't be friends. Jev seemed to hate all Reds.

48
00:03:57.779 --> 00:04:06.872
Well, not all Reds. Just then Gliss hurried out of the classroom, and Jev's voice instantly changed from sneering to sympathetic.

49
00:04:06.873 --> 00:04:11.370
"Hey, Gliss. Sorry your uncle is missing. Want me to walk you home?"

50
00:04:11.371 --> 00:04:15.198
"Thanks, that's sweet. But I'm in too much of a hurry to walk."

51
00:04:15.199 --> 00:04:21.089
Gliss rubbed her hands together and muttered the word "zap." A second later she disappeared.

52
00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:26.854
Jev frowned and then zapped himself away too. Zann was glad to see him go.

53
00:04:26.855 --> 00:04:33.964
"Come on," he told Perda. "I'll walk you home in case you're afraid of disappearing without a trace."

54
00:04:33.965 --> 00:04:37.500
"I'm not the one who should be afraid," she retorted.

55
00:04:37.501 --> 00:04:40.442
"The crow said the warning was only for Reds."

56
00:04:40.443 --> 00:04:44.617
"Okay," Zann said. "Then you can walk me home."

57
00:04:44.618 --> 00:04:47.801
She smiled. "It's a deal. Let's go."

58
00:04:47.802 --> 00:04:57.631
They headed for home. It was a bright, clear day with a light breeze that blew Perda's soft, caramel-colored hair around her face.

59
00:04:57.632 --> 00:05:01.474
Was it magic, or did she seem to get prettier every day?

60
00:05:01.475 --> 00:05:09.778
Zann tried not to notice that. It made him feel confused and nervous—a lot more nervous than he'd felt on hearing the echo crow's message.

61
00:05:09.779 --> 00:05:16.394
When they reached Perda's house, she sighed. "Looks like Mom's been redecorating again."

62
00:05:16.395 --> 00:05:23.564
The house had been square and blue that morning when the kids left for school. Now it was a multicolored blob.

63
00:05:23.565 --> 00:05:27.818
"Hey, she lives in Swamp Bottom, remember?" Zann joked.

64
00:05:27.819 --> 00:05:30.905
"She has to do something to lessen the boredom."

65
00:05:30.906 --> 00:05:34.975
Perda rolled her eyes. "See you tomorrow," she said.

66
00:05:34.976 --> 00:05:46.475
"Bye." Zann headed next door. His grandfather wasn't very interested in redecorating, so their house looked the same as always.

67
00:05:46.476 --> 00:05:50.703
In other words, it was just as boring as everything else in Swamp Bottom.

68
00:05:50.704 --> 00:05:54.628
For a second Zann wondered how his mother might redecorate the place.

69
00:05:54.629 --> 00:05:57.102
She'd always been good at that sort of thing.

70
00:05:57.103 --> 00:06:02.639
She'd loved to surprise him by turning his bedroom into a spooky cave or a mysterious jungle . . .

71
00:06:02.640 --> 00:06:06.775
He snapped out of those thoughts when he heard a rustling sound directly overhead.

72
00:06:06.776 --> 00:06:12.174
Glancing up, he barely had time to take in a dragon's snarling face hissing down at him.

73
00:06:12.175 --> 00:06:23.317
Zann jumped back just in time. A bolt of flame sizzled down, incinerating the ground where he'd just stood.
